# Campaign06 rendering failure

Actual launch session5015 exited1. Both investigator and author responses were received, paid usage accounted, and role parsing accepted. The first round then failed at rendering. Cleanup completed and idle-sleep protection was restored. No candidate reached evaluation; no critic or checkpoint completed.

Usage:2 calls,8,596 tokens,$0.04234. Campaigns03-06 combined:7 calls,27,713 tokens,$0.138295. Five calls and868,287 tokens remain. The approved conditional replacement requires at least six calls; that condition is false. No campaign07 may launch under the current grant.

The unchanged author response request09564719a54cfd10a0b6edbc5b61996e7a68015866f1e0b538859c542d158c0f has response-text SHA2c6d37ce6e8bc4eb65f021d70e289ac6c53612d7faba45c8ab1208489dad3d93. It uses base.__class__ and a generator expression. render_variants on the authenticated four-file parent reproduces ValueError: V5 policy AST contains an unbounded or stateful construct. See actual-render-failure.txt. No source execution, edited response, replay or test was used for diagnosis.

The source-format, qualified-symbol and mode repairs passed this time. The remaining architectural gap is that expected candidate-source rejection occurs before a materialized candidate exists and becomes a fatal rendering stage error. Existing invalid-experiment records can represent rejected proposals, but CandidateEvidenceV5 requires materialization and an all-invalid round currently aborts before feedback publication. This needs a deliberate runtime change, preserving sandbox restrictions and invalid/evaluated distinctions.

The investigator also lacks available entry-funnel counts. Actual parent reports show composite-score failures894-933 of960 rows per window and buy_signal_count0, but the investigator sees only four headline metrics per window. Gate counts overlap and do not alone prove causal necessity. Expose a bounded authenticated allowlist before another paid run.

No source change, image rebuild or new campaign preparation followed this failure. The requested two completed evaluated rounds and post-completion Luna handoff remain outstanding. A separate preparatory recovery plan will describe the work needed to reach them.
